  "readme": "# Text Your Mom\n\nText Your Mom is a playful consumer app that helps people stay close to family and friends by nudging them to reply, check in, and keep tiny relationship promises before avoidance turns into guilt.\n\n## Why This Example Works\n\n- Everybody knows the feeling of meaning to reply \"later\" and realizing it has been five days.\n- The product is emotionally real, funny, and easy to explain.\n- It gives the company a natural growth loop across TikTok, Reddit, and app product work.\n\n## Company Modules\n\n- [[company/strategy]]\n- [[company/goals]]\n- [[company/persona]]\n- [[company/kpis]]\n- [[marketing]]\n- [[app-development]]\n\n## Active Root Team\n\n- CEO for strategic alignment, executive communication, and subscription economics & runway\n- COO for operational reviews, process health, and technical direction & reliability\n\n## Child Cabinets\n\n- `marketing/tiktok` for short-form acquisition and creative testing\n- `marketing/reddit` for community insight, post experiments, and comment capture\n- `app-development` for roadmap, PRDs, quality, and release work\n\nThe root company cabinet is active. The child cabinets are installed as imported examples and remain paused until reviewed.",
